      "enrichment_notes": "The malicious classification for 198.51.100.77 substantially increases concern regarding this incident. As a known host-scanning and brute-force source, its presence directly aligns with the observed behavior: rapid credential guessing across multiple accounts (heavily targeting 'alice' alongside generic accounts like 'test', 'guest', and 'oracle') and endpoint enumeration (84 404s on /profile). Although the other three IPs (192.0.2.15, 192.0.2.16, 192.0.2.17) returned unknown reputations, they appear to be participating in coordinated or concurrent distributed credential attempts. Crucially, the presence of 3 successful logins in the same tight timeframe makes this incident critical to investigate immediately to verify whether any accounts were breached by the malicious IP or associated spray traffic.",
